    {"label":"Backup Power Investment Plan","type":"STRUCTURAL","evidence":"A","description":"Develop multi-year backup power plans incorporating generator capacity, transfer switch installation, critical circuit identification, and fuel storage requirements. Structured plans ensure comprehensive coverage without reactive over-spending after events.","cite":"NRCS CPS 372; ASABE EP460; NEC Article 702","target":"Structured planning -> comprehensive coverage -> prevented reactive over-spending"},
    {"label":"Power Resilience Valuation Culture","type":"CULTURE","evidence":"B","description":"Build management appreciation that backup power capability has quantifiable value in protecting biological assets (livestock), perishable products (milk, grain), and time-critical processes (ventilation, irrigation). Value awareness supports maintenance investment.","cite":"Journal of the ASFMRA, 2019 – Farm Risk Management Infrastructure","target":"Value appreciation -> maintained readiness -> protected high-value assets"},
    {"label":"Generator Operating Cost Calculator","type":"TOOLS","evidence":"A","description":"Implement operating cost calculators tracking fuel consumption, maintenance costs, and depreciation per hour of generator operation. Cost data enables accurate comparison between PTO generators, standby diesel units, and utility backup service options.","cite":"ASABE D497.7 – Agricultural Machinery Management Data","target":"Cost tracking -> technology comparison -> optimal backup power selection"}
